---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import { facts, portraitShot, site, stack } from "../data/site";
import Cta from "../components/Cta.astro";
import Manifest from "../components/Manifest.astro";
import Doc from "../layouts/Doc.astro";

const toc = [
  { id: "background", label: "01  BACKGROUND" },
  { id: "how", label: "02  HOW I WORK" },
  { id: "stack", label: "03  THE STACK" },
  { id: "where", label: "04  WHERE I AM" },
];

const meta = [
  { k: "BASED", v: "Bali · UTC+8" },
  { k: "REPLIES", v: "Same day" },
  { k: "SINCE", v: "5 years in production" },
  { k: "STATUS", v: "Available now", accent: true },
];
---

<Doc
  title={`About · ${site.name}`}
  description="Five years shipping production software across a blockchain company, a fintech and an agency, plus a competitive CTF background. One senior engineer, working remotely from Bali."
  ogType="profile"
  label="ABOUT"
  back={{ href: "/", label: site.name.toUpperCase() }}
  meta={meta}
  tocTitle="Contents"
  toc={toc}
>
  <Fragment slot="headline">
    <div class="eyebrow mb-[26px]">THE ENGINEER BEHIND THE SYSTEMS</div>
    <h1
      class="max-w-[860px] text-[clamp(42px,5.8vw,80px)] leading-[0.97] font-medium tracking-[-0.04em]"
    >
      <span class="line"><span data-line class="block">One engineer,</span></span>
      <span class="line"
        ><span data-line class="block">responsible <span class="text-mint">end to end</span>.</span
        ></span
      >
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-[30px] max-w-[620px] text-[18.5px] leading-[1.6] text-mute">
      I would rather own a whole system than a ticket in someone else's. That is what I am offering:
      one senior engineer who designs it, builds it, deploys it and is still there when it breaks.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <section id="background" class="scroll-mt-[90px]">
    <div class="eyebrow mb-5">01&nbsp;&nbsp;BACKGROUND</div>

    <div class="grid gap-8 sm:grid-cols-[300px_1fr]">
      <div>
        <div data-mask class="frame overflow-hidden p-0">
          <Image
            src={portraitShot}
            alt={site.name}
            widths={[300, 600]}
            sizes="(min-width: 640px) 300px, 92vw"
            class="h-[340px] contrast-[1.03] grayscale-[0.35]"
          />
        </div>
        <div class="figcap">
          <span>C. YU / BALI</span><span>FIG. 01</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <p data-reveal class="text-[17.5px] leading-[1.62] text-mute">
          I studied computer science and have spent five years shipping production software: a year
          at a blockchain company where mistakes are public and expensive, three at a fintech where
          the ledger has to balance every time, and a year at an agency where the deadline is the
          deadline.
        </p>
        <p data-reveal class="mt-5 text-[17.5px] leading-[1.62] text-mute">
          Three very different rooms, one job in all of them: make the thing work, and keep it
          working after launch week.
        </p>
        <p data-reveal class="mt-5 text-[17.5px] leading-[1.62] text-mute">
          Before any of it I played CTF competitively. A strange hobby that turned out to be useful:
          I spent years looking for the ways software breaks, so I write it differently. The
          security pass happens while the code is being written, not in an audit six months later.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="how" class="mt-[70px] scroll-mt-[90px] border-t border-line pt-[52px]">
    <div class="eyebrow mb-5">02&nbsp;&nbsp;HOW I WORK</div>
    <h2 data-reveal class="text-[34px] leading-[1.12] font-medium tracking-[-0.025em]">
      One person, the whole system.
    </h2>
    <p data-reveal class="mt-[22px] max-w-[680px] text-lg leading-[1.65] text-mute">
      I work remotely from Bali, on UTC+8. That is a full working day alongside Asia-Pacific and an
      afternoon-to-evening overlap with Europe and the UK, so a same-day reply is normal rather than
      a promise. Where the clock does not line up, I say so before we start rather than after.
    </p>
    <p data-reveal class="mt-[18px] max-w-[680px] text-lg leading-[1.65] text-mute">
      Everything on this site I designed, built and deployed myself. I build my own products because
      it is the fastest way to stay good at all of it: the interface, the schema, the deploy
      pipeline, the boring parts that decide whether software survives contact with users.
    </p>
    <p data-reveal class="mt-[18px] max-w-[680px] text-lg leading-[1.65] text-mute">
      You talk to the person writing the code. There is no account manager translating a brief into
      a ticket and back again, and nothing gets handed to someone you have not met.
      <a href="/systems" class="text-mint">How I think about architecture</a> is written down, and so
      is <a href="/services#how" class="text-mint">how a project actually runs</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="stack" class="mt-[70px] scroll-mt-[90px] border-t border-line pt-[52px]">
    <div class="eyebrow mb-5">03&nbsp;&nbsp;THE STACK</div>
    <h2 data-reveal class="text-[34px] leading-[1.12] font-medium tracking-[-0.025em]">
      One language, chosen so there is nothing to translate.
    </h2>
    <p data-reveal class="mt-[22px] max-w-[680px] text-lg leading-[1.65] text-mute">
      TypeScript from the database client to the browser, so a type defined once is enforced
      everywhere. The rest is deliberately unremarkable.
    </p>

    <Manifest rows={stack} class="mt-7" />
  </section>

  <section id="where" class="mt-[70px] scroll-mt-[90px] border-t border-line pt-[52px]">
    <div class="eyebrow mb-5">04&nbsp;&nbsp;WHERE I AM</div>
    <h2 data-reveal class="text-[34px] leading-[1.12] font-medium tracking-[-0.025em]">
      Remote, from Bali.
    </h2>

    <dl data-reveal class="hairgrid mono mt-7 text-[10.5px] sm:grid-cols-2">
      {
        facts.map((f) => (
          <div class:list={["px-4 py-3.5", f.wide && "sm:col-span-full"]}>
            <dt class="mb-1.5 text-dim">{f.label}</dt>
            <dd class:list={["m-0", f.accent && "text-mint", f.wide && "leading-[1.8]"]}>
              {f.value}
            </dd>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </dl>
  </section>

  <Cta heading="Tell me what you are building." />
</Doc>
